WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:06.960
The Season 5 finale of Game Of Thrones was
cliff-hanger central, leaving just about every

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.030
major plotline up in the air.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:13.440
So, what I'm going to do is talk about where
things could be headed in Season 6.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.340
This video is going to be all about the big
event, "For The Watch", and what that means

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.890
for the future of Jon Snow and the Night's
Watch.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:25.170
Just to give you a heads-up, there's going
to be speculation and possible spoilers for

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.380
the show and the books in this video!

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:33.750
Just before we start, in memory of Jon Snow,
our friends at Fun.com have given us a fantastic

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.292
Funko POP Vinyl figure to give away to awesome
viewers!

00:00:36.292 --> 00:00:42.070
All you need to do is be a subscriber and
leave a comment about Jon Snow or the Night's

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:44.280
Watch on this video.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:49.690
Jon Snow got Julius Caesar-ed, and he didn't
even see it coming!

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:55.049
He may have realised he was the 'most hated
man in Castle Black' but he still let Samwell

00:00:55.049 --> 00:00:59.540
Tarly leave him friendless, apart from Dolorous
Edd at the Wall.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:04.370
In the end, Jon Snow really did know nothing
– if he'd had any sense he'd have been using

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:08.640
the giant Wun Wun or Tormund the Wildling
as a bodyguard.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:13.610
There was loads of foreshadowing throughout
the season for who was going to stab Jon Snow:

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:20.420
all those glares from Olly and Jon deciding
to keep his enemy Alliser Thorne near rather

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:24.510
than send him off and Bowen Marsh appeared
as well!

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:29.000
Oh, and by the way, it was interesting that
Alliser Thorne stabbed Jon 'For The Watch'

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.909
as when Ser Alliser was leading the Watch
during the battle of Castle Black in Season

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:39.030
4 he told Jon that "leadership means being
second-guessed by twats".

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:43.620
Well, it seems like Ser Alliser's been doing
quite a lot of his own second-guessing this

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.800
season about Jon's decision to work with the
Wildlings to save the Watch and everyone else

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.010
from the White Walkers.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:55.770
I wonder how long he and the Night's Watch
will live to regret that fact next season?!

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:00.320
The way For The Watch happened reminded me
of Janos Slynt's beheading…

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:06.530
Jon hesitated at first but then Jon's face
screwed up when Slynt said how afraid he was,

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.960
and Jon beheaded him.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:13.330
Olly was also hesitant at first, but when
Jon said Olly's name, the young boy also screwed

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.220
up his face &amp; stabbed Jon hard.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:21.540
There were also shades of Red Wedding about
Jon's death, which was similar to Robb Stark's

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.540
end.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:29.080
Probably not a coincidence given this episode
was directed by David Nutter, who also directed

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.590
The Red Wedding episode.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:35.420
On a side note, the way Arya killed Meryn
Trant also reminded me of how Catelyn Stark

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:40.330
killed Walder Frey's wife and how she was
ultimately killed herself, with a slit to

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:41.480
the throat.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:46.069
Jon's death also made me think of Ned Stark's
death, especially because of the constant

00:02:46.069 --> 00:02:49.290
parallels that have been drawn between Jon
and Ned this season.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:54.209
For example, Stannis told Jon that 'you're
as stubborn and honourable as your father.'

00:02:54.209 --> 00:02:57.569
Jon replied, 'I can imagine no higher praise.'

00:02:57.569 --> 00:03:00.410
To which Stannis said, 'I didn't mean it as
praise.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.750
Honour got your father killed.'

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:08.140
Straight after the season 5 finale Entertainment
Weekly released an interview with Kit Harington

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:10.740
who plays Jon Snow.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.260
In it they asked him "Is Jon really dead?"

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.840
Now he replied "This is my understanding of
it."

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:23.190
He also said "If anything in the future is
not like that, then I don't know about it

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.980
– it's only in David and Dan and George's
heads."

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:33.240
And he added "I'm not coming back next season
and I'm looking for movies for next year."

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:38.220
That's fine, it doesn't mean his character's
out of the show forever, because as we know

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:44.110
they skipped storylines and seasons for Isaac
Hempstead-Wright as Bran and everyone else

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:49.610
in that storyline wasn't in season 5 but they
will be returning for season 6.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:56.560
Of course, he could still be filming for season
6, but given all the leaks during films, it'd

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:00.069
be really difficult to keep his return under
wraps if he is filming at any point this year

00:04:00.069 --> 00:04:01.069
for Season 6.

00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:04.349
Maybe he won't be in Season 6 a lot and he's
shot some stuff already.

00:04:04.349 --> 00:04:08.349
Also another little thing from the interview
that made me think he's returning is he didn't

00:04:08.349 --> 00:04:15.569
get a parting gift, like Rose Leslie, who
played Ygritte did.

00:04:15.569 --> 00:04:21.539
Wouldn't be the first time an actor had to
be creative with the truth to avoid spoiling

00:04:21.539 --> 00:04:23.409
major plot points in an interview.

00:04:23.409 --> 00:04:29.820
Still, there are ways that Jon Snow could
return and fulfil Samwell Tarly's words that

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:33.630
"I've been worrying about Jon for years; he
always comes back."

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:38.469
First of all, the Red Woman, Melisandre, has
returned to Castle Black.

00:04:38.469 --> 00:04:40.909
In fact, in the books, she never left.

00:04:40.909 --> 00:04:46.749
And, like Thoros of Myr did with Beric Dondarrion,
it's possible that she could bring Jon Snow

00:04:46.749 --> 00:04:53.219
back to life with the power of the Lord of
Light.

00:04:53.219 --> 00:05:01.559
Now, when someone's brought back to life there
are side effects for example a person loses

00:05:01.559 --> 00:05:07.080
some of their memories and is less themselves,
as Beric Dondarrion told Arya in Season 3.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:13.339
So, maybe Jon Snow won't be exactly the Jon
Snow we know, in other words, he'll be "someone

00:05:13.339 --> 00:05:14.339
else…

00:05:14.339 --> 00:05:17.580
something else", like Oliver Queen in Arrow!

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:22.599
And the fact that Jon is stabbed beside a
cross adds to the vibe that he's going to

00:05:22.599 --> 00:05:24.840
have a Christ-like resurrection.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:28.000
Another possibility is that Jon wargs into
Ghost.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:33.479
Now, in the TV show, we didn't see Jon's direwolf
at the end of the episode when he's attacked.

00:05:33.479 --> 00:05:38.469
However, in the books, as Jon is stabbed by
his fellow Night's Watchmen he says the word

00:05:38.469 --> 00:05:39.469
"Ghost".

00:05:39.469 --> 00:05:44.639
But remember episode 7 this season, when some
Night's Watch men attacked Gilly and taunted

00:05:44.639 --> 00:05:49.060
Sam by saying, "Your friend Jon Snow's not
here now".

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.490
And who appeared right at that moment?

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.330
Yes, it was Ghost.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:59.389
So, both the show and the book seem to be
hinting that Jon Snow might warg into Ghost.

00:05:59.389 --> 00:06:04.210
and, during a Q&amp;A event at Oxford University,
Kit Harington said that he'd like to be a

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:07.240
warg and 'put himself into a wolf'!

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:12.319
To which, Dan Weiss replied, 'Two words for
you: Season 6.'

00:06:12.319 --> 00:06:14.430
And there's another possibility…

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:18.100
Remember when we saw the White Walkers and
the Night's King during the Hardhome episode?

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:22.569
Well, there was a definite Night's Watch vibe
to their clothing worn.

00:06:22.569 --> 00:06:27.620
Dressing the White Walkers like Men in Black
in the show is likely a nod to book readers

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:33.030
that the Night's King in the series is also
a former Lord Commander of the Night's Watch!

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:39.279
All of which makes me wonder if the fact that
one of the Wildlings called Jon "King Crow"

00:06:39.279 --> 00:06:43.090
means that something more is going to happen
between Jon and the Night's King?

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:48.139
And there was also that long lingering look
between the Night's King and Jon Snow, just

00:06:48.139 --> 00:06:54.270
before the chief Iceman raised his arms and
with them his horde of new wildling wights!

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:59.620
Was it just one former Lord Commander, the
Night's King, observing the new Lord Commander

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:00.620
Jon Snow?

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:05.639
Or could it be that the Night's King isn't
just a former Lord Commander, but Jon's long-lost

00:07:05.639 --> 00:07:09.180
uncle and fellow Night's Watchman, Benjen
Stark?

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:15.039
And, could Jon be reanimated to the Night's
King's band of walkers and wights?

00:07:15.039 --> 00:07:19.210
But what if Jon Snow were actually, horror
of horrors, dead?!

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:24.849
Well, then he'd just be the latest in a long
line of Starks to kick the bucket in nasty,

00:07:24.849 --> 00:07:25.909
treacherous circumstances.

00:07:25.909 --> 00:07:31.729
And I mean it's not like Game Of Thrones hasn't
killed off big characters in the past.

00:07:31.729 --> 00:07:36.910
So, have all the apparent foreshadowing for
Jon's come-back in the show just been red

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:37.910
herrings?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:38.910
It's entirely possible.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:44.330
After all, there have been others, and everyone
from Kit Harington to John Bradley, the episode's

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:50.439
director David Nutter and the showrunners
are doing interviews saying that John is dead!

00:07:50.439 --> 00:07:55.569
And the official HBO viewer guide says that
Olly "conspired with other brothers to murder

00:07:55.569 --> 00:07:58.029
[Jon Snow], and delivered the fatal cut."

00:07:58.029 --> 00:08:00.259
So, are we just in denial?

00:08:00.259 --> 00:08:02.719
Say it ain't so!!

00:08:02.719 --> 00:08:07.449
Of course, just like they skipped Bran's storyline
this season, there's always a chance they

00:08:07.449 --> 00:08:10.439
leave the Watch and the Wall until season
7.

00:08:10.439 --> 00:08:15.030
Samwell and Gilly are on their way to Old
Town where he wants to become a Maester, like

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.959
Maester Aemon, who died this season.

00:08:17.959 --> 00:08:21.189
Samwell's already killed a White Walker with
dragonglass.

00:08:21.189 --> 00:08:26.629
And the show seems to be foreshadowing Sam's
future importance again in the battle against

00:08:26.629 --> 00:08:31.949
the White Walkers as Samwell told Jon that
at the citadel's library he'd be able to "learn

00:08:31.949 --> 00:08:37.560
about history, strategy, healing, and other
things, things that'll help when they come."

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:42.500
So, will Sam discover a treasure trove of
dragonglass or Valyrian steel from his readings

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:43.500
at the Citadel?

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:47.940
So, those are my thoughts on what might happen
for Jon Snow in Season 6.

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:51.110
Do you think Jon's really dead?

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:53.330
If not, how would you like him to return?

